 "trace": {
  "calibration": "172 diagram: 69.82 px/m along (face px 59, end 1708 = 23.62 m), 81.43 px/m up",
  "model.cab": "cab door 1.046-2.077; door 1 centred 6.51, door 2 17.337 (two-leaf, 1.64 wide as the 170's: panes 0.308-0.766 from the centre); cab-car windows [2.277,3.079], [3.452,5.228], [7.791,9.61], [9.94,11.759], [12.088,13.907], [14.237,16.056], [18.619,20.438], [20.768,22.587]; bogies 3.32, 20.19 (wheel 0.76 and wheelbase 2.0 kept from the old model: unverified)",
  "model.next": "doors centred 6.266, 17.094 from its inner end; windows at the cab car's pattern (not read)",
  "model.heights": "as the 171 diagram (same shell family): bottom 0.967, cantrail line 3.28, roof 3.77, glass 1.995-2.90: not read on a 172 photo",
  "model.face": "172342 head-on (Stourbridge, 460 px/m): the gangwayed 172/2-3 front (27 of 39 units; every 172 photographed 2024-2026 is WMR): gangway frame +-0.51 y 1.02-3.56 (depth ~0.3 from photos; the diagram's 0.59 not used), yellow door +-0.37 y 1.08-3.23, screen glass m 0.53-1.17 y 1.98-3.27 (the dark surround drawn 3 cm round it), one black sloped lamp box a side (0.57,1.255), (0.61,1.535), (0.87,1.68), (1.14,1.71), (1.12,1.40), head m 0.954 y 1.50 r 0.125 outboard, LED m 0.715 y 1.42 r 0.08; wiper pivot (0.90,2.04) tip (0.55,2.68); number on the near side m 0.92 y 1.84; the face gold above, black lower front below 1.0 (pwor, p342)",
  "liveries.LM": "WMR: overcast pwor samples: purple body purple-wor #423935, gold cab end gold-wor #9E511B to the cab door's rear edge (photo wins over the diagram's 3.49 m), gold doors face-wor #C47424 (door-wor is a reflection, iqr 73), face gold face-wor #C47424, gangway door yellow-wor #D7940A, lower front black-wor #222220, roof roof-wor /2.5; the gold diamonds fading into purple behind the cab and the roof-dome LED not drawn",
  "notes": "The 172/0-1 (12 units, non-gangwayed) not drawn as a variant: WMR's 172s are mostly /2-/3.",
  "model.cab.windows.photo": "pwor (172220, the near side seen with the nose right): FIVE windows between the doors, not the diagram's four. Read by a 1D projective fit along the bodyside through door 1's and door 2's edges (residuals 2.4-4.6 cm): [7.76,9.44], [9.64,11.25], [11.45,13.0], [13.21,14.69], [14.8,16.31]. The windows ahead of door 1 and behind door 2 are the diagram's (extrapolated readings unreliable). The next car's five assumed the same, moved with its doors",
  "liveries.LM.branding": "the one-line 'West Midlands Railway' wordmark (the published LM.svg is the stacked logo with diamonds, not what the 172 carries; pwor and psh are too small to trace): traced from the WMR 172 diagram (dia: 69.82 px/m from the face at px 59, 81.43 px/m up from rail row 340) as two pieces in their own colours, lilac-white 'West Midlands' (px 782-909, rows 208-221: 10.36-12.17 m, 1.46-1.62 m) and orange 'Railway' (917-979, 208-225: 12.29-13.18 m, 1.41-1.62 m); pwor (lg172) shows it in the same place under the windows (not measured there)",
  "liveries.LM.diamonds": "the gold diamonds: the diagram's orange (221,88,0) regions in the purple at the cab end (px 298-360) and the car end (1590-1660), each drawn as the diamond of its bounding box (8 at the front, 9 at the rear); the front group sits at the gold/purple boundary, which the diagram draws at 3.42 m and the photo at 2.077 m (the cab door's rear edge, photo wins), so moved 1.343 m forward with it; colour the face gold #C47424",
  "liveries.branding.next": "the second car is a mirrored driving car: branding repeated at the mirrored position (length minus x), not measured on that car"
 },
